From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:50:15 +1300
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3576-armsom-cm5-io: let TCPM own the USB-C
 VBUS

vcc_5v0_typec0 is the switched VBUS of the USB-C port. It is the
FUSB302 vbus-supply, and also the phy-supply of u2phy0_otg. The PHY
enables it at boot and keeps it on, so TCPM never sees vSafe0V and a
sink partner stays in SRC_ATTACH_WAIT. A USB-C dock is not detected.

Drop the phy-supply and leave VBUS to TCPM, as the vendor DTS does.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261024083942.148860-1-gahing@gahingwoo.com/
Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5-io.dts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5-io.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5-io.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5-io.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-cm5-io.dts
@@ -307,7 +307,6 @@ &u2phy0 {
 };
 
 &u2phy0_otg {
-	phy-supply = <&vcc_5v0_typec0>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-- 
Armbian

